   },
   {
    "_type": "box",
    "_key": "e2178c1",
    "cls": "e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent",
    "children": [
     {
      "_key": "ffd18da",
      "cls": "elementor-widget-heading",
      "_type": "heading",
      "tag": "p",
      "html": "Dental Implant FAQs"
     },
     {
      "_key": "eb7165e",
      "cls": "elementor-widget-n-accordion",
      "_type": "accordion",
      "items": [
       {
        "_key": "dc932d9",
        "title": "How long do dental implants last?",
        "open": true,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "dc932d9",
         "cls": "e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "c9c03df",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>With proper care and regular checkups, dental implants can last 20 years or more—often a lifetime. They’re one of the most durable tooth replacement options available.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "b56b014",
        "title": "Does getting a dental implant hurt?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "b56b014",
         "cls": "e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "6f45e62",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>The procedure is typically done under local anesthesia, with sedation options available for added comfort. Most patients report minimal discomfort during recovery, often less than a tooth extraction.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "40b7933",
        "title": "What is the cost of dental implants in Santa Clarita?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "40b7933",
         "cls": "e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "c1a813d",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>Costs vary depending on your specific treatment plan. At Valencia Smile Expert, we offer transparent pricing, flexible financing, and a detailed breakdown before treatment begins.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "6aeb3fd",
        "title": "How long does it take to get dental implants?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "6aeb3fd",
         "cls": "e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "d6207cf",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>The full process can take a few months, depending on healing and any preparatory treatments like bone grafting. However, same-day implants may be possible in select cases.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "0d65776",
        "title": "Are dental implants safe for seniors?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "0d65776",
         "cls": "e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "152f699",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>Yes. Dental implants are a safe, effective option for older adults in good overall health and with sufficient bone density—or those open to bone grafting.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "_key": "ca452da",
        "title": "What’s the difference between dental implants and dentures?",
        "open": false,
        "content": {
         "_type": "box",
         "_key": "ca452da",
         "cls": "e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-child",
         "children": [
          {
           "_key": "5cea510",
           "cls": "elementor-widget-text-editor",
           "_type": "text",
           "html": "<p>Dental implants are permanent fixtures that integrate with your jawbone, providing a stable, natural-feeling replacement for missing teeth. Unlike traditional dentures, they don’t slip, don’t require adhesives, and help prevent bone loss over time.</p>"
          }
         ]
        }
       }
      ],
